# RELEASE W2 · THE PACKAGING SEAM (DIAMOND-RELEASE-CANDIDATE.md)
# npm law: a `files` array in the ROOT package.json VOIDS the root .npmignore for
# every path beneath a files-covered directory — but a NESTED .npmignore (this file)
# is honored for its own subtree. This is the template SCP's tarball boundary.
#
# NOTE: this is .npmignore, NOT .gitignore — the SCP keeps its OWN git (the
# separate-repo design; see .gitignore beside this file). This file only shapes
# what ships inside the npm tarball.

# Runtime bridge state — created fresh by the SCP + the CLI at run time
# (mkdir recursive on every write). The dev copy carries a dev userCwd.
Cascades/Bridge/

# Dev session working documents — never user-facing.
Cascades/Working/

# The turn-over heartbeat — CLONE_SKIP_FILES already skips it at install;
# finalizeScpInstall seeds it fresh (the C248 seed law).
.bridge-restart.json

# Cadmium Researcher runtime research data — regenerated per install; the
# structural files (S8.json · menu.json · topics.json · assets · targeted demo)
# still ship.
Cascades/Extended/*/frontier/
Cascades/Extended/*/Cascades/

# Build + dependency artifacts (safety — the root .npmignore's intent, made real).
dist/
node_modules/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
